        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\n> If I write `#` in insert mode a space should be automatically added after like `# `. Same with other comments like `// `.\n> \n> For css files if I write `/*` it should expand to `/* */` with cursor in the middle.\n\nThis behavior is a bit too intrusive and I feel will be more inconvenience than otherwise. So this will not be a 'mini.comment' feature (default or otherwise). Although it *might* be possible in the future after 'mini.keymap' is released.\n\n> If I visual select a word in css and write `gciw` it should surround just that word in a comment.\n\n'mini.comment' only [supports per line commenting](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/581724ebb39f4aa70bdbffb891d57d6141d29035/doc/mini-comment.txt#L21) due to lack of a robust/built-in way to infer the correct structure of not per-line commenting.\n\nClosing as not planned (at least partially and not in 'mini.comment')",
