        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Is there reason it's too intrusive isn't it the expected way to do comments? I can't find plugin that can do it.\n\nWhat part of the issue are you referring to? The \"For css files if I write `/*` it should expand to `/* */` with cursor in the middle\" part? If yes, then commenting plugins are (traditionally) mostly concerned with converting lines between being commented and not commented.\n\nThis behavior is more in the snippets/abbreviations territory. You can have this manually set up by putting something like this in '~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/css.lua':\n\n```lua\nlocal maybe_expand_comment = function()\n  local line_before_cursor = vim.fn.getline('.'):sub(1, vim.fn.col('.'))\n  if line_before_cursor:sub(-1) ~= '/' then return '*' end\n  return '*  */<Left><Left><Left>'\nend\nvim.keymap.set('i', '*', maybe_expand_comment, { expr = true, desc = 'Maybe expand comment' })\n```\n",
